        "original_id": "96406703-033e-5466-a768-91835a662784",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Candy, John Hughes, Mel Brooks, Bill Pullman, Rick Moranis, Daphne Zuniga, Dick Van Patten, Joan Rivers\n- Works: Planes, Trains and Automobiles, Spaceballs\n- Roles: Del Griffith\n\nFacts:\n- John Franklin Candy was born on October 31, 1950, and he was a Canadian actor and comedian known mainly for his work in Hollywood films.\n- Planes, Trains and Automobiles is a 1987 American comedy film written, produced, and directed by John Hughes.\n- John Candy gave one of his most renowned onscreen performances as Del Griffith, a loquacious traveling shower-curtain ring salesman, in the John Hughes comedy Planes, Trains and Automobiles.\n- Spaceballs stars Mel Brooks, Bill Pullman, John Candy, and Rick Moranis, and it also features Daphne Zuniga, Dick Van Patten, and the voice of Joan Rivers.\n- John Franklin Candy died on March 4, 1994.",
